{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts","id":1345693,"title":"Alchemicals vs Solars and other Creation-exalts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-03T20:24:06-08:00","id":1345693,"title":"Alchemicals vs Solars and other Creation-exalts","content":"So its something I saw on the 'Ask the Unconquered Sun' thread. <br /> <br /> Autobot asked if he could go to Creation and asked to watch out for the alchemical exalted. <br /> <br /> Sol asked why he would worry about the alchemical exalted, since each exalted cost vast amounts of resources, could only use a set number of charms at a time, and took a large amount of time to replace. <br /> <br /> So here's the thing. I kinda agree. And yet, it irks me. I love solars, don't get me wrong. But Alchemicals are incredibly fascinating, both in the fact that they're far more dependent on human intervention than other exalts, their ability to switch out charms, the magitech and steampunk aesthetics, as well as their focus, not on ruling humans, but facilitating them. <br /> <br /> So on this comparism of Alchemicals vs Solars... what advantages do Alchemicals have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T20:41:04-08:00","id":1345696,"title":"","content":"I think you already said it. The ability to swap out charms is massive and shouldn't be understated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T20:53:05-08:00","id":1345697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345696#post1345696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you already said it. The ability to swap out charms is massive and shouldn't be understated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... yes, but Solars can simply learn whatever charms they need, and each charm requires vast amounts of resources, not just to build, but also to design and implement. Vat complexes ain't cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:01:35-08:00","id":1345699,"title":"","content":"Personally, I tend to view the &quot;load-out&quot; mechanic as more of a disadvantage than an advantage. I mean, sure they can swap their Charms out so one day they can be loaded out with social Charms and the next day they can be loaded out with combat Charms, but a Solar doesn't have to worry about that. After they spend exp to learn a Charm they just always have access to that Charm. They're loaded out with their combat Charms and social Charms and craft Charms and every other Charm they've learned every single day of the week. Meanwhile (at least in 2nd edition) the Alchemical spends slightly less exp per Charm, but if he doesn't have those Charms equipped than he simply doesn't have access to them at all.<br /> <br /> This also came with the drawback that Alchemicals needed to spend exp on &quot;slots&quot; in order to equip the Charms they spent exp on, and then needed to commit Essence on top of that to actually equip the Charms, which functionally put two caps on how many Charms they had access to (I remember Holden mentioning he wanted to change or get rid of one of both of those mechanics in 3rd edition when he got around to dealing with Alchemicals, but I don't know what the current writers and dev have planned.) And, of course, there's the issue that it's very difficult to swap Charms out on the fly - if you want to change your loadout it generally requires you to go back to a base of operations with a vat complex, which could take days or weeks or might not even be possible at all (if you find yourself in the Far Reaches of Autochthon, in Creation, or somewhere else).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying is a bad mechanic, I think it's actually pretty cool and it makes the Alchemical play experience very different from a Solars, but overall it's one that I definitely consider to be much more disadvantageous than advantageous.<br /> <br /> They also turn into giant living warstriders and eventually cities, which is really fucking cool, but I don't know if I would necessarily consider that an 'advantage' over a Solar (who has a much easier time operating on a normal human scale at high Essence).<br /> <br /> Ultimately I think Alchemicals are really fucking awesome, but I don't know that they necessarily have many mechanical advantages over Solars. That's okay though, they don't necessarily <i>need</i> mechanical advantages over Solars. Their &quot;advantages&quot; are more a matter of roleplaying (similar to Dragon Blooded) and generally rests more in their place in society. They're respected heroes who are cheered on by adoring crowds whereas Solars are generally hunted and forced into hiding. They also have more easy access to artifacts and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-04-2019, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:15:04-08:00","id":1345702,"title":"","content":"In general, you won't tend to find any exalt with a real kind of advantage over Solars. They're the most powerful, it's in the description.<br /> <br /> A Dragonblooded general can summon a thunderstorm, call down lightning, and raise the earth into fortifications in an instant, but they're not actually better than a Solar general for it. Lunar shapeshifting is probably the closest you'll ever get, and it's only because it gives Lunars a really wide variety of base abilities that they can really easily get without focusing.<br /> <br /> If you just want to win a fight, cure a disease, convince somebody of something, the Solar who's good at that thing will do it better than anyone else. On the other hand Solars can't become living cities with badass steampunk avatars walking around either, or casually engulf an entire battlefield in fire, or shapeshift into a hundred different animals. You'll notice that the list of things they simply can't do though has nothing to do with the result, just the way they do it.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of really fun and super cool ways of doing things that Solars will never get to do, but they'll never be better than doing it the Solar way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:16:32-08:00","id":1345704,"title":"","content":"I mean, a good thing I think is when Alchemicals actually have forewarning on what they're up against. You get a bunch of alchemicals, all kitted out for social, and you drop invincible sword princess on them? Dead alchemicals. <br /> <br /> You get a dozen alchemicals, kit them out with combat charms, and throw them at invincible sword princess? You've got stuff working out for you. And because you can make more alchemicals (while solars are capped at 150/300), eventually, a solar gets mobbed. <br /> <br /> Things also come out for rulers, too. A ruler may distrust a solar. After all, their charms are all self-contained, solars may eventually learn charms to mind control and whip up the masses, and basically may supplant the ruler. No such thing for alchemicals. I mean, they may be dangerous, they may be powerful, but they're capped by the fact that they need mortal industry. A ruler, forced to choose between a solar/ dragonblooded and an alchemical, may simply opt to have the alchemical and ply them with a vat complex and various artifacts/ charms and resources to improve them, reasoning that an expensive and hard to maintain vat complex and alchemical charms is a better and more reliable use of their resources than a solar or dragonblooded that may take the money and turn against them anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T23:09:51-08:00","id":1345715,"title":"","content":"Just because you can make more Alchemicals doesn't mean doing so isn't <i>ruinously expensive</i>. It'd be like saying the Rebels blowing up the Death Star was no big deal because the Empire was capable of building another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T00:52:16-08:00","id":1345724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345715#post1345715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you can make more Alchemicals doesn't mean doing so isn't <i>ruinously expensive</i>. It'd be like saying the Rebels blowing up the Death Star was no big deal because the Empire was capable of building another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But compared to, what, Solars? You can't control who gets a solar exaltation. And try as you might, you'll never replicate one. <br /> <br /> But an alchemical exalted, on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:06:01-08:00","id":1345726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345724#post1345724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But an alchemical exalted, on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>An Alchemical, on the other hand, requires a soul of sufficient heroism, having unflinchingly proved its merit over multiple incarnations through word and deed.<br /> <br /> \u200bThose ain't exactly in abundant supply either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:40:57-08:00","id":1345729,"title":"","content":"In theory if you had access to hundreds of billions of souls and an unlimited supply of the magical materials you might be able to make tens of thousands of Exalted (assuming you don't need anything else such as some level of Autochthon's intervention) but that seems well outside the current scope of the setting to the point that it's sort of getting into individual homebrew setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:24:52-08:00","id":1345736,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345699#post1345699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I tend to view the &quot;load-out&quot; mechanic as more of a disadvantage than an advantage. I mean, sure they can swap their Charms out so one day they can be loaded out with social Charms and the next day they can be loaded out with combat Charms, but a Solar doesn't have to worry about that. After they spend exp to learn a Charm they just always have access to that Charm. They're loaded out with their combat Charms and social Charms and craft Charms and every other Charm they've learned every single day of the week.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think the main distinction was supposed to come from how it's more expensive for a Solar to diversify to that degree. And not just in terms of the costs of their Charms, which was higher than those of Alchemicals; a Solar that wants to go deep into any of those cascades is going to run into needing a maximized Ability very quickly.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alchemicals technically need high Attributes as well sure, but a thing that I feel that people often forget was how they got an Augmentation Charm that could increase their Attributes. Alchemicals weren't just about changing loadouts for their Charms, but for their Attributes as well to ensure that they had the minimums for those Charms. It wasn't unlimited, but I think that on the whole it would work out as less expensive for the Alchemical than buying the Attribute dots wholesale (at the cost of taking up some Charm slots), the Attributes also not being too expensive to buy.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Between that and the fact that there are fewer Attributes than Abilities, in practical terms I think it was generally supposed to be easier and more expected for an Alchemical to have a more diverse set of options than a typical Solar would have, just constrained within the terms of not being able to do all of it at once. I expect an Alchemical to switch between a high level of capability in combat, social and creative endeavours than I do a Solar.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That being said, sure I wouldn't regard this as an advantage as such, it's just an element of characterisation. You express a lot of a Solar through their Abilities, and even a Lunar through their Attributes, but for an Alchemical the minimums they need for Charms aren't really a big deal and aren't the primary way of depicting them; this would be why their Charms aren't even organised by Attribute cascades. Alchemicals are expressed through their context and function, and their personal decisions in how they pursue these things.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345702#post1345702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, you won't tend to find any exalt with a real kind of advantage over Solars. They're the most powerful, it's in the description.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345702#post1345702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Dragonblooded general can summon a thunderstorm, call down lightning, and raise the earth into fortifications in an instant, but they're not actually better than a Solar general for it. Lunar shapeshifting is probably the closest you'll ever get, and it's only because it gives Lunars a really wide variety of base abilities that they can really easily get without focusing.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, given the Charms, Lunars have better things to compare to Solars now.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dragon Blooded and Lunars do have specific things that they can do that Solars can't. A Solar is not disadvantaged by the lack of these things in the way that, say, a Terrestrial is disadvantaged by having nothing that can take away the disadvantage of Legendary Size or a Lunar might be stifled by the lack of things dedicated to interacting with complex organisations. But they are still afforded some tactical avenues and general means of pursuing an endeavour that Solars do lack, and a Solar character/player might be jealous of them having the option.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345715#post1345715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you can make more Alchemicals doesn't mean doing so isn't <i>ruinously expensive</i>. It'd be like saying the Rebels blowing up the Death Star was no big deal because the Empire was capable of building another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, the Death Star seems to be limited more by construction time than budget. I understand that the Expanded Universe depicted the Empire as being an authoritarian, totalitarian regime that still mostly allowed the gigantic corporations to manage their own affairs (and indeed, unregulated) in a manner that still makes for a robust economy providing plenty of resources, which the autocratic ruler can draw upon with impunity. It might be really expensive to build another Death Star, but it's not as if the Emperor or military needs approval from a Senate appropriations committee for it to be added to the budget, there are implicitly a lot of welfare state expenses that the Empire neglects as a matter of course in favour of military spending, and if large sections of the astronomically large population are oppressed to ensure that there isn't deficit spending, well... they were going to be anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T06:46:08-08:00","id":1345761,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can't beat solars by out-muscling them. You need to find a niche you can exploit. The big advantage lunars have is they can easily become competent in everything, which means they will probably have an area or two where they can outperform any given solar, since the latter tend to be more specialists. Alchemicals have a similar advantage, being attribute-based too. <br /> <br /> What they'd need to do is know who they were dealing with in advance, and select a charm loadout that attacks the solar in question's weak points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T07:49:13-08:00","id":1345767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345736#post1345736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dragon Blooded and Lunars do have specific things that they can do that Solars can't. A Solar is not disadvantaged by the lack of these things in the way that, say, a Terrestrial is disadvantaged by having nothing that can take away the disadvantage of Legendary Size or a Lunar might be stifled by the lack of things dedicated to interacting with complex organisations. But they are still afforded some tactical avenues and general means of pursuing an endeavour that Solars do lack, and a Solar character/player might be jealous of them having the option.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>They have some, and in very specific situations they might be better. Like if there\u2019s a huge theee dimensional maze where you can\u2019t touch any of the surfaces, a lot of Lunars are just going to breeze through that, and Solars aren\u2019t. Those tend to be edge cases though, where the way you do things is really advantageous, as opposed to just the end result.<br /> <br /> Lunars get a lot of cool powerful charms that let them manipulate emotions and enforce/destroy cultural norms, but Solars just get a bunch of bonuses to do whatever they want. Earth Dragonblooded are really good at resisting seduction attempts, Solars are just amazing at resisting all social influence.I think it makes other types of exalted really interesting and fun to play, but it doesn\u2019t really give them a leg up. Even in their wheelhouse they tend to be more or less as good as a Solar who\u2019s using her charms to do a very similar thing. <br /> <br /> Which certainly isn\u2019t to say that Solars can\u2019t be beaten in their area of expertise, but unless you\u2019re another Solar your advantages are coming from somewhere other than your exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T08:08:31-08:00","id":1345769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345761#post1345761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can't beat solars by out-muscling them. You need to find a niche you can exploit. The big advantage lunars have is they can easily become competent in everything, which means they will probably have an area or two where they can outperform any given solar, since the latter tend to be more specialists. Alchemicals have a similar advantage, being attribute-based too. <br /> <br /> What they'd need to do is know who they were dealing with in advance, and select a charm loadout that attacks the solar in question's weak points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think this is a simplified aspirational statement that doesn't fully reflect the practical manner in which the game's mechanics play out.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;you can't outmuscle a Solar&quot; might be an accurate statement in the sense of not being able to build a towards yielding superior numbers with equal resources, but a lot of the time it feels like saying that it's impossible to win in a fight against a Solar, which seems to have had various levels of accuracy across Editions.<br /> <br /> The intention in this system at least seems to be that a Solar is not so advantaged against somebody in a similar arena that they can't be overcome with a good sequence of decision making and favourable outcomes in any of the random parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345767#post1345767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesn\u2019t really give them a leg up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say it did. Don't think it matters. Asking the wrong questions. Still have specific powers that aren't really in the Solar wheelhouse; I don't really see 'em inflicting horrible insanity on people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless you\u2019re another Solar your advantages are coming from somewhere other than your exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does being smart about how you apply your Charms (in the sense of decisions about what order to use them in) fall under that umbrella?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:55:17-08:00","id":1345792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345699#post1345699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I tend to view the &quot;load-out&quot; mechanic as more of a disadvantage than an advantage. I mean, sure they can swap their Charms out so one day they can be loaded out with social Charms and the next day they can be loaded out with combat Charms, but a Solar doesn't have to worry about that. After they spend exp to learn a Charm they just always have access to that Charm. They're loaded out with their combat Charms and social Charms and craft Charms and every other Charm they've learned every single day of the week. Meanwhile (at least in 2nd edition) the Alchemical spends slightly less exp per Charm, but if he doesn't have those Charms equipped than he simply doesn't have access to them at all.<br /> <br /> This also came with the drawback that Alchemicals needed to spend exp on &quot;slots&quot; in order to equip the Charms they spent exp on, and then needed to commit Essence on top of that to actually equip the Charms, which functionally put two caps on how many Charms they had access to (I remember Holden mentioning he wanted to change or get rid of one of both of those mechanics in 3rd edition when he got around to dealing with Alchemicals, but I don't know what the current writers and dev have planned.) And, of course, there's the issue that it's very difficult to swap Charms out on the fly - if you want to change your loadout it generally requires you to go back to a base of operations with a vat complex, which could take days or weeks or might not even be possible at all (if you find yourself in the Far Reaches of Autochthon, in Creation, or somewhere else).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypothetical design idea: What if every Alchemical Charm in the book were always completely available to every Alchemical? Charms then become the product of state industry rather than things individually attuned to particular Alchemicals (and thus no longer an XP expense for characters). Now, what they use is a matter of personal preference, planning, available Charm slots, and Essence and Attribute ratings.<br /> <br /> If that wouldn't produce enough mechanical differentiation from other Alchemicals, you could also flag certain Charms with tags like Moonsilver or Jade, making Essence rating requirements for Charms that particularly resonate with certain magical materials more easily available for some members of an Assembly than others, sort of like a Supernal function for Alchemicals. Then the Soulsteel Caste could more easily pick up Personality Override Spike while the Moonsilver Caste gets first access to Magnetic Joint Bearings.<br /> <br /> Also, mobile vat complexes need to be a thing, either something that can either be moved about with vehicles and powered with elemental cores - probably requiring days of assembly to be functional and the same to be able to be packed for moving - or else a Charm that would let Collossus Alchemicals service their Champion kin. Otherwise, the character refit logistics of wars between the Eight Nations become ridiculous for PCs, who would end up trapped for extended periods without ability to swap around their Charm load outs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:09:23-08:00","id":1345798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345769#post1345769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't say it did. Don't think it matters. Asking the wrong questions. Still have specific powers that aren't really in the Solar wheelhouse; I don't really see 'em inflicting horrible insanity on people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they don\u2019t do that for sure. Or even further out there what about a charm that lets you inflict a mental disease that spreads like a plague. That\u2019s AWESOME but what are you really trying to do with it? Destabilize a court so that you can take it over? If that\u2019s the case a Solar could almost certainly do that faster and more efficiently through their own solar mightiness. If you\u2019re thinking \u201cwho cares how cool the inflicting insanity way is if it\u2019s not better.\u201d then probably just don\u2019t play anything but a Solar. <br /> <br /> If you\u2019re facing a problem and wondering what kind of exalt would be best suited to fixing it, the answer is almost, but not quite always, a Solar. If it\u2019s not a solar it\u2019s usually because of setting reasons rather than abilities. <br /> <br /> In another game you might be able to go \u201cah-ha! Solars may be powerful, but the Lunars are exalted of wild things. So here in the primordial woods, with tangling vines underfoot and choking spores in the air, it is the Lunars that have the advantage over the Solars!\u201d but not in Exalted. Dipping Swallow doesn\u2019t just ignore penalties due to non-wilderness related things, it ignores all penalties from any source in any amount. The Lunar might have the advantage there, but it would be because that specific Solar didn\u2019t take the charms required to fight in those conditions, and the Lunar did, not because the Solar ones are worse or non-existent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345769#post1345769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does being smart about how you apply your Charms (in the sense of decisions about what order to use them in) fall under that umbrella?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely say yes. You can be smart about how you spend your essence. A stupidly arrogant Solar might decide that their Lunar opponent isn\u2019t worth the effort of expending much spiritual power on, and then by the time he realizes his mistake his back is broken by the primordial beast-god that he decided to engage in combat. They could also be the exact opposite, spending every last mote on the first turn of combat, and then the clever Lunar somehow blocks it or it turns out that they joined battle against an illusion or something and now the Solar is exhausted when the fresh Lunar charges in. <br /> <br /> Or they might just be at a flat tactical disadvantage, like a Solar sword fighter in heavy armor against a Wood Dragon cavalry archer. Without some very specific charms that Solar will simply never catch the DB. Mechanically the Solar there is at -2 to his roll to chase and the DB is at +4, before charms, which I\u2019m willing to say isn\u2019t just a mechanical quirk but something that could absolutely show up in the setting where mechanics aren\u2019t the physics engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:19:57-08:00","id":1345803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345792#post1345792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, mobile vat complexes need to be a thing, either something that can either be moved about with vehicles and powered with elemental cores - probably requiring days of assembly to be functional and the same to be able to be packed for moving - or else a Charm that would let Collossus Alchemicals service their Champion kin. Otherwise, the character refit logistics of wars between the Eight Nations become ridiculous for PCs, who would end up trapped for extended periods without ability to swap around their Charm load outs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that refit times for alchemicals and their charms is way too long, and that you think they should be shorter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:25:07-08:00","id":1345807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345792#post1345792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hypothetical design idea: *buckets of awesome*</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. If Alchemicals don't end up working like this then I'm going to be severely disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:28:27-08:00","id":1345809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345807#post1345807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. If Alchemicals don't end up working like this then I'm going to be severely disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect nothing. <br /> <br /> Or maybe we can ask the devs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:55:08-08:00","id":1345817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345803#post1345803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that refit times for alchemicals and their charms is way too long, and that you think they should be shorter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like speaking for others, but unless you're trying to evoke Jordan Peterson, I don't think that's what's being said.<br /> <br /> Refit times are okay. Spending three months travelling home from a warzone, getting refitted, then spending three months travelling back to the warzone is what takes too long.<br /> <br /> Instead you should pull back an hour's travel to your forward command base, get refitted overnight for tomorrow's mission then get redeployed in the morning fit for action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:01:30-08:00","id":1345819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345817#post1345817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like speaking for others, but unless you're trying to evoke Jordan Peterson, I don't think that's what's being said.<br /> <br /> Refit times are okay. Spending three months travelling home from a warzone, getting refitted, then spending three months travelling back to the warzone is what takes too long.<br /> <br /> Instead you should pull back an hour's travel to your forward command base, get refitted overnight for tomorrow's mission then get redeployed in the morning fit for action.</div> </div> </div> </div>*scratches head*<br /> <br /> Ok, tell me if I'm wrong, but does it take a long-ass time on the level of a month or so to refit and alter your charm loadout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:19:00-08:00","id":1345821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345819#post1345819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*scratches head*<br /> <br /> Ok, tell me if I'm wrong, but does it take a long-ass time on the level of a month or so to refit and alter your charm loadout?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably -- I think you're thinking about regrowing a destroyed Charm, but I don't actually remember how long it used to take (I want to say 5 hours per Charm, but it could be months, I don't remember). <br /> <br /> But that's still a secondary concern compared to not being able to swap your Charms without a Vats Complex, and only having a Vats Complex in a friendly city (which itself is an Essence 8+ Exalt) hundreds of miles away, if not thousands of miles away... at best across no-mans-land, if not across actively hostile territory... <i>if</i> there even is one in your dimensional plane of existence.<br /> <br /> My point is, you need to actually <i>be able</i> to swap your Charms -- 2E made simply being eligible to swap too difficult, never mind the actual process. (And I think that was Kyeudo's point.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-04-2019, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:19:16-08:00","id":1345822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345819#post1345819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*scratches head*<br /> <br /> Ok, tell me if I'm wrong, but does it take a long-ass time on the level of a month or so to refit and alter your charm loadout?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all logistical. You need the Vats to redo your Charm loadout, right? If so, 'how long it takes to alter your Charm loadout' really boils down to 'how close are the nearest Vats'? Depending on variables, it could take overnight (IIRC, swapping out Charms is about 1 hour per?), or it could literally take months.<br /> <br /> The first obvious issue is that, AFAWK, there are no Alchemical Exalted in Creation until they break the Seal. The implication is that there are no Vats in Creation. So... how good are the Eight Nations at logistics? In the <i>general</i> case, I'd say pretty good. They should understand the concept. But they may not really comprehend the <i>nature</i> of the logistics they need.<br /> <br /> If you play the Alchemicals' entering of Creation as a war--as the default explanation, at least in past Editions--then you have to ask, 'What are the Alchemicals doing?' If they're meant to be Chthonic-Army Knives, then you <i>need the Vats to be accessible</i>. If they're not, then you hamstring the Alchemicals' flexibility. From a gameplay perspective, you're quite literally removing one of the advantages of the Alchemicals if you reduce their flexibility.<br /> <br /> So... this all hinges on the requirements of the Vats. Presumably, you would set them up in Manses. Which you would have to either find or take over, and then repurpose. If you do that, then you can have a <i>very</i> nice campaign (in both the war and role-playing senses) as the Eight Nations/Alchemicals are constantly trying to take Manses to essentially shorten their supply lines for their Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> I mean, historically, you can look at Operation Barbarossa to see the impact of logistics on a war effort. (There are any number of any other examples.) Substitute Alchemicals for Panzer Divisions, and dragon lines for rail lines, and... there you go.<br /> <br /> If you envision a more peaceful first contact situation, then you would still see the Eight Nations negotiating for Manses as the most likely place to refit their Champions. <br /> <br /> So... I mean, from a Goals perspective, calling it the Locus Crusade made a bit of sense, but from a less strategic perspective, I think I prefer 'The Dragon Line War'.<br /> <br /> There's also the slight concern that if the Eight Nations start converting a lot of manses to Vat-complexes or something similar... will Autochthon start overwriting Gaea/Creation? What's going to happen then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:29:20-08:00","id":1345825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345792#post1345792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Otherwise, the character refit logistics of wars between the Eight Nations become ridiculous for PCs, who would end up trapped for extended periods without ability to swap around their Charm load outs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wars between the Eight Nations consist of flash raids. If an Alchemical is fitted out to function like a tactical bomber, they can't remain in the air indefinitely. Fortunately, they can also be fitted to function as a commando.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345798#post1345798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they don\u2019t do that for sure. Or even further out there what about a charm that lets you inflict a mental disease that spreads like a plague. That\u2019s AWESOME but what are you really trying to do with it? Destabilize a court so that you can take it over? If that\u2019s the case a Solar could almost certainly do that faster and more efficiently through their own solar mightiness. If you\u2019re thinking \u201cwho cares how cool the inflicting insanity way is if it\u2019s not better.\u201d then probably just don\u2019t play anything but a Solar. <br /> <br /> If you\u2019re facing a problem and wondering what kind of exalt would be best suited to fixing it, the answer is almost, but not quite always, a Solar. If it\u2019s not a solar it\u2019s usually because of setting reasons rather than abilities. <br /> <br /> In another game you might be able to go \u201cah-ha! Solars may be powerful, but the Lunars are exalted of wild things. So here in the primordial woods, with tangling vines underfoot and choking spores in the air, it is the Lunars that have the advantage over the Solars!\u201d but not in Exalted. Dipping Swallow doesn\u2019t just ignore penalties due to non-wilderness related things, it ignores all penalties from any source in any amount. The Lunar might have the advantage there, but it would be because that specific Solar didn\u2019t take the charms required to fight in those conditions, and the Lunar did, not because the Solar ones are worse or non-existent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't listening to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would definitely say yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the distinction is meaningless to gameplay and characterisation, and that people constrain their story scenarios and charger interactions when they focus to much on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:43:30-08:00","id":1345830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345821#post1345821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably -- I think you're thinking about regrowing a destroyed Charm, but I don't actually remember how long it used to take (I want to say 5 hours per Charm, but it could be months, I don't remember).<br /> <br /> But that's still a secondary concern compared to not being able to swap your Charms without a Vats Complex, and only having a Vats Complex in a friendly city (which itself is an Essence 8+ Exalt) hundreds of miles away, if not thousands of miles away... at best across no-mans-land, if not across actively hostile territory... <i>if</i> there even is one in your dimensional plane of existence.<br /> <br /> My point is, you need to actually <i>be able</i> to swap your Charms -- 2E made simply being eligible to swap too difficult, never mind the actual process. (And I think that was Kyeudo's point.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Just checked. Nope. Just takes a few hours to several days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:11:21-08:00","id":1345838,"title":"","content":"So back on cost, should an alchemical be considered something on the level of a fighter jet, or a carrier, in terms of resource cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:14:06-08:00","id":1345839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345838#post1345838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So back on cost, should an alchemical be considered something on the level of a fighter jet, or a carrier, in terms of resource cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the price of a heroic soul? What is it to have Autochthon breathe a spark of life into a body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:16:11-08:00","id":1345842,"title":"","content":"Hmm... probably somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> Most nations have several dozen Alchemicals, IIRC. Even in WW2, the richest nations on earth didn't have dozens of aircraft carriers (I think?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:49:28-08:00","id":1345848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345839#post1345839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the price of a heroic soul? What is it to have Autochthon breathe a spark of life into a body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:53:05-08:00","id":1345850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345839#post1345839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the price of a heroic soul? What is it to have Autochthon breathe a spark of life into a body?</div> </div> </div> </div>What?! Come on, Alchemicals are still made of actual scarce resources, the fact that their creation needs to be budgeted is an explicit part of the books.<br /> <br /> Hell, they're described as being often made in bulk because it's cheaper to undergo the process with many at once than doing it one at a time.<br /> <br /> Accelerator, the creation of Alchemical Exalted is described as the kind of thing that can put a smaller nation into debt for years. If say that's more akin to the costs of an aircraft carrier, with the caveat that these economies are working on a smaller scale in which making an Exalt is a severe expense even if it doesn't actually cost what an aircraft carrier does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345842#post1345842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most nations have several dozen Alchemicals, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>At about a thousand Exalted in total, you're looking at an average between 120 and 130.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in WW2, the richest nations on earth didn't have dozens of aircraft carriers (I think?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, keep in mind that none of the Octet have needed to build all of their Alchemicals at once. No aircraft carrier has lasted for three or four thousand years. Their maintenance is probably not ruinous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:56:34-08:00","id":1345853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345848#post1345848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that both are rare enough to make the notion you've presented, where casualties on the side of the Alchemicals are less of a factor than when those losses occur on the side of Creation's Exalted, is not all that workable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345850#post1345850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?!</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345850#post1345850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on, Alchemicals are still made of actual scarce resources, the fact that their creation needs to be budgeted is an explicit part of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm pretty sure I expressed such pretty early on. But the book <i>also </i>indicates that a meritorious soul is needed to catalyze an Alchemical. It doesn't matter if Yugash has a billion tons of orichalcum at hand, if that heroic spark is not there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-04-2019, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:02:16-08:00","id":1345860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345842#post1345842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... probably somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> Most nations have several dozen Alchemicals, IIRC. Even in WW2, the richest nations on earth didn't have dozens of aircraft carriers (I think?).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several mitigating circumstances. <br /> <br /> 1. Apparently one of the reasons Alchemicals are so expensive is because not only is there large amounts of magical materials, but also clay. Clay rare in the realm of brass and shadow. And, well, on any other place it would be easy to get clay. <br /> <br /> 2. No need for maintenance. Let's face it. Metal rusts. Wires rot. Things get stuck. Parts need replacement. A carrier is paid for once, and repaid for continuously because exposure to time and the sea means that you need a literal army of technicians and maintenance workers to make sure it doesn't fall apart. And even then, metal fatigue sets in. With an alchemical, not so much. Do nothing with it, and it'll just eat, sleep, talk.<br /> <br /> 3. Personnel for usage. I mean, don't get me wrong. Alchemical exalted need hundreds of trained men to be refitted and used. But that's one time. An aircraft carrier working? That's 6000 personnel. On the ship. And you'll need to pay them and feed them. And make sure they don't go stir crazy.<br /> <br /> 4. Usage. Aircraft carriers are powerful... But limited. There ain't much use for the inland. An alchemical exalted, though... He can write national policy. He can assassinate a leader. He can write subliminal songs to induce loyalty. He can carry out feats of coordination and such fsr beyond mortal ken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:16:12-08:00","id":1345863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345803#post1345803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that refit times for alchemicals and their charms is way too long, and that you think they should be shorter?</div> </div> </div> </div>JohnDoe244 already covered the gist of my opinion. Certainly I think a hour per charm swapped would be better than five hours, but when it comes to vat time for raising Attributes, Essence, and adding Charm slots, the travel times from and back to the front are quickly going to exceed the &quot;training&quot; times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345825#post1345825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wars between the Eight Nations consist of flash raids. If an Alchemical is fitted out to function like a tactical bomber, they can't remain in the air indefinitely. Fortunately, they can also be fitted to function as a commando.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to reread CoCD:Autochthonia. The various wars described aren't one time raids, but concerted campaigns against each other. You don't get the absolute hatred that leads to raising a lost village to hate their former nation and turn them into sleeper saboteurs out of just periodic raiding, nor do you so threaten one of the oldest Alchemical cities that it decides to drop a quarter of the city upon the invaders without large numbers and serious support behind your infantry rather than respond with less sacrificial means such as paramagnetically hurled cargo containers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:30:14-08:00","id":1345866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345825#post1345825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't listening to me.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I re-read your post a few times and I\u2019m still not getting it. Do you mean that inflicting insanity as an end all to itself Amadeus Arkham style is when Lunars find it easier?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345825#post1345825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the distinction is meaningless to gameplay and characterisation, and that people constrain their story scenarios and charger interactions when they focus to much on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s meaningless. It\u2019s not like Solars are generally more stupid with their tactics than anyone else. Sometimes they can have a lot of restraint and finesse. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s good if people understand it though because it could lead to bad expectations otherwise. If you didn\u2019t know that you might think that your Dragonblooded Air aspect can do this really clever thing where he challenges a Dawn to an archery duel, but he\u2019s got an ace up his sleeve, he\u2019s guarenteed that on the day of the fight there will be a legendary thunderstorm. Dragonblooded get a major edge when fighting in harsh conditions, so you might think that in that fight it would help even the odds. It doesn\u2019t though, Solar evasion and Archery magic not only also gets to ignore the harsh weather, but often does so better. <br /> <br /> If you\u2019re going into that fight and your life depends on it, don\u2019t go in like that. Make sure you\u2019re a much more experienced archer, or goad her into being completely over confidant. Or even forget honour and just set a trap where you and your hearth ambush her. You can\u2019t go there thinking that because you\u2019re in your wheelhouse that you can match a Solar blow for blow. I\u2019m not even saying you\u2019ll lose, but the odds aren\u2019t good.<br /> <br /> Lunars have it way better because they\u2019re already much closer to a Solar in their abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:20:15-08:00","id":1345890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345798#post1345798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In another game you might be able to go \u201cah-ha! Solars may be powerful, but the Lunars are exalted of wild things. So here in the primordial woods, with tangling vines underfoot and choking spores in the air, it is the Lunars that have the advantage over the Solars!\u201d but not in Exalted. Dipping Swallow doesn\u2019t just ignore penalties due to non-wilderness related things, it ignores all penalties from any source in any amount. The Lunar might have the advantage there, but it would be because that specific Solar didn\u2019t take the charms required to fight in those conditions, and the Lunar did, not because the Solar ones are worse or non-existent.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a tangent to that, my impression would be that (if 3e Lunars balance has gone as it should!) this is true... but that the Solar player has had to build for that quite strongly, and the incentives of Solar Caste and archetypes probably don't generally push for that (covering a far wider array of bases and personalities which are often mutually exclusive with this). So in practical purposes, this situation often perhaps does play out more along these lines in above quote marks? For all that it is imaginable that a player *could* design a Solar such to oppose this situation, for most practical PCs, Lunars are often likely to have the advantage in that scenario? (E.g. it is more likely that the situation would in general play out in that way than it wouldn't, for all that in some platonic sense where you imagine equal amounts of abstract character development/pacing resource that &quot;exists&quot; only OoC, the Solar is in some sense still &quot;best&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:43:28-08:00","id":1345926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345853#post1345853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And I'm pretty sure I expressed such pretty early on. But the book <i>also </i>indicates that a meritorious soul is needed to catalyze an Alchemical. It doesn't matter if Yugash has a billion tons of orichalcum at hand, if that heroic spark is not there.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> \u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's not an answer to the question that was asked.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345860#post1345860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. No need for maintenance. Let's face it. Metal rusts. Wires rot. Things get stuck. Parts need replacement. A carrier is paid for once, and repaid for continuously because exposure to time and the sea means that you need a literal army of technicians and maintenance workers to make sure it doesn't fall apart. And even then, metal fatigue sets in. With an alchemical, not so much. Do nothing with it, and it'll just eat, sleep, talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but... nobody makes an Alchemical with the intention that they'll do nothing.<br /> <br /> The... let's call them comparative maintenance costs are probably lower than a large vehicle, but they're not nothing. An Alchemical's Charms need to be constructed, their body requires refits when their Attributes or Essence are increased, and while they do heal naturally, performing maintenance with them in the vats heals them a lot more quickly, and the Nations generally want their Champions in top condition at all times, so they're liable to go for the quickest healing route available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345863#post1345863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The various wars described aren't one time raids, but concerted campaigns against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Campaigns to what objective?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get the absolute hatred that leads to raising a lost village to hate their former nation and turn them into sleeper saboteurs out of just periodic raiding, nor do you so threaten one of the oldest Alchemical cities that it decides to drop a quarter of the city upon the invaders without large numbers and serious support behind your infantry rather than respond with less sacrificial means such as paramagnetically hurled cargo containers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are both outliers. Holden was always very emphatic about how the Elemental War was something unique and dreadful in the history of Autochthonia, a war driven by nationalistic fervour and hatred rather than the acquisition of resources. Lux employing that means to fight off the invaders from Jarish was something that took place during the period of religious warfare between the Eight Nations prior to them agreeing on things like the standardised caste system thousands of years in the setting's past. It was also a tactic driven less by pragmatic need than by the city's legendary ego.<br /> <br /> It's hard to sustain something like wars of conquest when everybody has to pass through tunnels to get at one another and there's often no sure way to tell how long your nations are going to be actually next to each other.<br /> <br /> If one has the pdf, just doing a word search on &quot;raid&quot; will keep bringing one to the point of how the standard way that the nations relate to each other martially is through raiding for people and resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345866#post1345866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I re-read your post a few times and I\u2019m still not getting it. Do you mean that inflicting insanity as an end all to itself Amadeus Arkham style is when Lunars find it easier?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I do not mean inflicting the kinds of psychological damage that they can out of some kind of devotion to mental illness. I mean wanting to get a person to engage in that specific sustained pattern of behaviour, or wanting to hurt them in that particular manner.<br /> <br /> I'm coming at this not in terms of approaching it like there's a set of objectives that has to be achieved however, and achieving such makes basically any means of doing so equivalent. I'm imagining in terms of people and how they relate to one another and experience things.<br /> <br /> Although that being said, I'm also referring to Charms that sustain themselves over time without mote commitments and gradually destroy all of a person's other Intimacies. Even if considering things solely in terms of an end result of a person having no Intimacies besides obsession over you (that is to say, not considering the lack of cost over time and need to personally engage at all times), that's a result even a Solar would find challenging.<br /> <br /> I'm not in this for the matter of figuring out who is better, but if you are then I'll ask you to consider whether or not a Solar needing to commit more attention, time and energy to a result might actually constitute being less good at it.<br /> <br /> But that's not what I'm here for. I have no interest in devising a tier list, I'm concerned with the fine details and the tone of the different kinds of stories that the Exalted tell. Lunars having Charms to inflict (the unfortunately named) Derangements gives them a tone that Solars lack, as inflicting derangements through their own Charms isn't really their bag. Dragon Blooded having an Investigation Charm meaning that attempting to harm them while they've been invited into your home is stopped by a variety of elemental manifestations gives them a tone that Solars lack, because not only do their powers generally not deal in drawing in such external manifestations, they don't really have anything with such absolute effects.<br /> <br /> (The Eclipse Anima isn't something that all Castes can learn)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s meaningless. It\u2019s not like Solars are generally more stupid with their tactics than anyone else. Sometimes they can have a lot of restraint and finesse.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I find objectionable and concerning is when people describe the notion of two Exalted fighting as though it's like those martial arts movies where the combatants face across one another and play out the entire battle in their minds, perfectly and equally predicting all of the moves and countermoves ahead of time, and reaching an indelible conclusion that means that they don't even bother with the fight.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they do, and it just plays out exactly as they both predicted.<br /> <br /> Yes, a Solar character/player will be engaging in their own tactical play. That's supposed to make the fight exciting and dynamic and capable of unexpected steps (if not necessarily unexpected outcomes) that make it worth engaging in. I would hope that there's enough of a probability curve in the dice, enough variety in the tactics afforded by Charms, just enough fallibility in the players (in terms of things like their resource management and what they're willing to commit to a given fight), and a Storyteller willing to throw in the odd complication that can shake a fight up a bit as to make it worth engaging in.<br /> <br /> That and beneficial outcomes that are not absolute, but can be capitalised on later. Hopefully not too much later if the point of the fight was to, say, make the Solar use up their Seven Shadow Evasion so that they won't have the option when it might have been really needed later on in the scene. That can include circumstances in which the Solar didn't quite need to use it when they did, and weren't thinking of the future (which I think should be something that a Solar controlled by a Storyteller as an antagonist for Dragon Blooded is slightly more liable to, in the interests of sustaining a story).<br /> <br /> I mean jeez, has nobody ever played a Solar that burnt up a lot of their Initiative using Heavenly Guardian Defence to stop a bad damage roll, and then a bad withering attack came in to crash them, and then they were set upon by a decently equipped battle group?<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that there might be and should be means by which somebody less powerful than a Solar is capable of having a victory against a Solar in terms more sophisticated than bringing their kryptonite or conducting the battle in the one environment in which you're rolling higher numbers. Keeping in mind that &quot;a victory&quot; need not mean &quot;killed them this time&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:09:08-08:00","id":1345954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345926#post1345926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Campaigns to what objective?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the very, very long history of Autochthonia, I suspect every objective that humans have attempted to accomplish via warfare has been tried. Economic, social, political, religious, ideological, territorial, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those are both outliers. Holden was always very emphatic about how the Elemental War was something unique and dreadful in the history of Autochthonia, a war driven by nationalistic fervour and hatred rather than the acquisition of resources. </div> </div> </div>Holden hasn't done enough looking at human history then. War driven by nationalistic fervor has been around as long as the concept of nations. Given the political models of Authochthonia (nationalistic propaganda, centralized planning, authoritarian caste systems, low value on human life), I would expect more nationalistic wars there, not less. The Elemental War would just be the most recent one and couple itself with expressions of Autochthon's sicking body due to his long slumber aggravated by the damage caused by nation-scale conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lux employing that means to fight off the invaders from Jarish was something that took place during the period of religious warfare between the Eight Nations prior to them agreeing on things like the standardised caste system thousands of years in the setting's past. It was also a tactic driven less by pragmatic need than by the city's legendary ego. </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. The city cut off the equivalent of its arm just to show off and hasn't managed to fully recover in thousands of years. I'm not buying that. You only resort to such tactics when flinging men around like toothpicks and other abilities available to a gigantic paramagnetically suspended city won't get the job done. Jarish needed to be fielding a force big enough and dangerous enough to threaten the city in a meaningful way, not a smash-and-grab raiding party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's hard to sustain something like wars of conquest when everybody has to pass through tunnels to get at one another and there's often no sure way to tell how long your nations are going to be actually next to each other. </div> </div> </div>Hard, yes, but not impossible. Estasia believed it could pull such things off multiple times and still contemplates more attempts. The setting even describes some of the signs that plates will begin parting and the process is usually slow instead of the violence seen at the end of the Elemental War.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If one has the pdf, just doing a word search on &quot;raid&quot; will keep bringing one to the point of how the standard way that the nations relate to each other martially is through raiding for people and resources. </div> </div> </div>Even a war over resources is going to require extended time in the field. The kinds of things that the Octet war over aren't grain or cattle - food comes out of the walls in Autochthonia after all - but instead over metals, clays, and other hefty things that need to be excavated and transported. When seizing resources, the ground needs to be held long enough for the pillagers to do their work against enemies operating on shorter supply lines. Forward depots of material are going to be critical to war logistics just like they continue to be in our modern age. Alchemicals are the military equivalent of tanks - getting them refitted for a mission and back in the field is going to be key to success and if your enemy can specialize an Alchemical for a mission in three days, you need the ability to match that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:24:21-08:00","id":1345958,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I meant point two &lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345860#post1345860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are several mitigating circumstances.<br /> <br /> 1. Apparently one of the reasons Alchemicals are so expensive is because not only is there large amounts of magical materials, but also clay. Clay rare in the realm of brass and shadow. And, well, on any other place it would be easy to get clay.<br /> <br /> 2. No need for maintenance. Let's face it. Metal rusts. Wires rot. Things get stuck. Parts need replacement. A carrier is paid for once, and repaid for continuously because exposure to time and the sea means that you need a literal army of technicians and maintenance workers to make sure it doesn't fall apart. And even then, metal fatigue sets in. With an alchemical, not so much. Do nothing with it, and it'll just eat, sleep, talk.<br /> <br /> 3. Personnel for usage. I mean, don't get me wrong. Alchemical exalted need hundreds of trained men to be refitted and used. But that's one time. An aircraft carrier working? That's 6000 personnel. On the ship. And you'll need to pay them and feed them. And make sure they don't go stir crazy.<br /> <br /> 4. Usage. Aircraft carriers are powerful... But limited. There ain't much use for the inland. An alchemical exalted, though... He can write national policy. He can assassinate a leader. He can write subliminal songs to induce loyalty. He can carry out feats of coordination and such fsr beyond mortal ken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point 2 is especially important in the context that ALchemicals, while I doubt very few have lived that long probably do regularly go around for a few centuries, meanign a few layers of overlap there in ages and years that cause build-up. We'd have a lot more carriers for the US if every single oen we made and not lost in a battle were still in tact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 11-04-2019, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:32:37-08:00","id":1345980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345958#post1345958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I meant point two &lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Point 2 is especially important in the context that ALchemicals, while I doubt very few have lived that long probably do regularly go around for a few centuries, meanign a few layers of overlap there in ages and years that cause build-up. We'd have a lot more carriers for the US if every single oen we made and not lost in a battle were still in tact.</div> </div> </div> </div>And helps alchemicals survive. I mean, how many machines have entire armies and governments built, only for those same war machines to fall to rot and decay as the budget was grafted, stolen, or just plain redirected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:35:11-08:00","id":1345982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345954#post1345954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the very, very long history of Autochthonia, I suspect every objective that humans have attempted to accomplish via warfare has been tried. Economic, social, political, religious, ideological, territorial, etc.<br /> <br /> Holden hasn't done enough looking at human history then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compass: Autochthonia may have fudged realism a bit in pursuit of goals based on genre conceits and creating an environment that intertwined the familiar with the alien but, well, welcome to Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. The city cut off the equivalent of its arm just to show off and hasn't managed to fully recover in thousands of years. I'm not buying that. You only resort to such tactics when flinging men around like toothpicks and other abilities available to a gigantic paramagnetically suspended city won't get the job done. Jarish needed to be fielding a force big enough and dangerous enough to threaten the city in a meaningful way, not a smash-and-grab raiding party.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're shifting the goalposts away from &quot;read what's in the book&quot; to &quot;I don't actually buy into what the book depicts&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, on top of Lux consistently being portrayed as quite the little giant city diva, and the idea of a grandiose hero opting for a dramatic and showy method over the practical one (see <b>the very fact that Lux has paramagnetic catapults in the first place </b> as opposed to... bridges), you're just kind of overlooking details such as it being a described as a last resort tactic at a time when the city's usual defences had been shut down (a good faith reading of that might conclude that flinging regular projectiles was off the table) and, again, Estasia was facing a war that was unlike the norm for conflict within the limiting confines of the Realm of Brass and Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard, yes, but not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard is good enough to make something uncommon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Estasia believed it could pull such things off multiple times and still contemplates more attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And always failed.<br /> <br /> Nations are not wholly rational actors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kinds of things that the Octet war over aren't grain or cattle - food comes out of the walls in Autochthonia after all</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't come out of every wall, and even if it did, that wouldn't mean there is no value in possessing a surplus while also denying rivals the same.<br /> <br /> Like, of barrels of slurry are easier to carry then pallets of steel, and you steal them from people that will pay you steel to get back the slurry (because people need to eat every day and time spent increasing production of slurry is time taken away from some other industry), which might the raiders go for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but instead over metals, clays, and other hefty things that need to be excavated and transported.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excavated? Why are they attacking mines instead of warehouses?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When seizing resources, the ground needs to be held long enough for the pillagers to do their work against enemies operating on shorter supply lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shorter supply lines are generally why you don't want to be locked down in one place. If you're going after something that will take long enough to load up that enemies will surround you, you're doing residing incorrectly.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not as if we lack historical example of this. Vikings, Saracens, the Anglo-Scottish border, pastoral nomads out of China's northern frontier, all examples of societies that enriched themselves on a sustained process of using high mobility and good planning to get in, grab lots of valuable materials and people, then get out before an enemy force could be mobilised against them and cut off their line of retreat.<br /> <br /> True, in many of these cases, sustained campaigns of raising gradually evolved into straight up colonisation, but the Scandinavians were a bit dependent on things like Britain not eventually being completely inaccessible from Scandinavia. It also being a lot more accessible owing to the fact that there is a while sea to sail across, rather than being to approach via tunnels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forward depots of material are going to be critical to war logistics just like they continue to be in our modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some kinds of operations. Lightning raids still function today, facilitated by things like planes. They're not concerned with the acquisition of commodities, but their opposition have advantages that Autochthonians will generally lack, such as wider implementation of more accurate and destructive ranged weaponry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals are the military equivalent of tanks - getting them refitted for a mission and back in the field is going to be key to success and if your enemy can specialize an Alchemical for a mission in three days, you need the ability to match that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemicals can be the military equivalent of a lot of things. Sometimes they're commandos, where you outfit them for stealth, speed and precision that increases the time they can stay ahead of and harass enemies before they need to go back to the vats. Maybe they sometimes go outfitted for maximum destruction because the person planning the raid decided to go for a blitzkrieg approach, all &quot;go in and obliterate everything, sustain fire while the troops pick up the goods and then fall back&quot;. Maybe there's an Alchemical build that is the equivalent of anti-armour rockets, but if it takes three days for them to get there then a viable tactic is to not be there anymore. Retreat into those tunnels that are hard to be followed into and easier to set traps in. Perhaps use your blasty powers to cave in the entrance.<br /> <br /> Or send a second Alchemical prepared to counter the skirmisher in defence of the blaster, I don't know.<br /> <br /> Sure these are all gambles. That's what war is; at any given time, a range of tactical and strategic options where good intelligence shortens the list but never reduces the options down to one, and where any given option can turn out to be a mistake only at the point where it makes contact with the enemy (for reasons that couldn't be guessed prior to that contact). Decisions that are almost always made within a set of logistics constraints.<br /> <br /> Compass: Autochthonian depicts a world where a fairly uniform resource constraint is the inability to mobilise the vats needed for Exalted to respec, so they need to plan around that. When they're at war for resources, they're not conducting one raid, but as many as they can get. They all have to be planned within the constraints of limited personnel and resources, which are likely to be different for each raid. A good start is to not select a target where the time it will take you to get what you need will get you surrounded. If you want resources that will take longer to pull out, your logistics constraints probably make it often smarter to send another raid whose objective is to draw attention away to create a wider window around your actual target than try and establish a beach head. And even if a beach head is established, it's one that you're going to abandon once you have everything you need and the nations are going to drift apart.<br /> <br /> If it's a war over something else... are commando raids not the better option for purposes of sabotage and assassination?<br /> <br /> It's going to be hard in any event to have pitched battles in this world, there is often not the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:42:01-08:00","id":1345987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345890#post1345890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is more likely that the situation would in general play out in that way than it wouldn't, for all that in some platonic sense where you imagine equal amounts of abstract character development/pacing resource that &quot;exists&quot; only OoC, the Solar is in some sense still &quot;best&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...kind of. You're certainly more likely to find enemies who are taking advantage of their own powers, that's for sure. The thing is, if you're playing a Solar, you don't really need to do that. You don't need to set up a situation where your powers work best, because they always work best. Lunars have a neat charm for when they violate a custom of a culture to reflexively roll to try and convince everyone to overlook the slight. Solars have a charm that just makes them never commit a faux pas in the first place, no roll needed.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a 2m charm to half defense penalties against an enemy, or completely ignore them from enemies with lower initiative. Solars have a charm for the same cost that ignores all penalties regardless of initiative, and rewards 1i for successfully blocking. Also it costs only 1m if Fivefold Bulwark Stance is active. Solar doesn't worry about what initiative she's at, she just puts up the barrier and it always works.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this isn't Schrodinger's Solar. If you're a Solar swordsman, you have Dipping Swallow Defense is a Melee 1, Essence 1, Zero prerequisite charm. It's just better to be a Solar, at least in terms of achieving victory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345926#post1345926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not what I'm here for. I have no interest in devising a tier list, I'm concerned with the fine details and the tone of the different kinds of stories that the Exalted tell. Lunars having Charms to inflict (the unfortunately named) Derangements gives them a tone that Solars lack, as inflicting derangements through their own Charms isn't really their bag. Dragon Blooded having an Investigation Charm meaning that attempting to harm them while they've been invited into your home is stopped by a variety of elemental manifestations gives them a tone that Solars lack, because not only do their powers generally not deal in drawing in such external manifestations, they don't really have anything with such absolute effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 110% with you on the different exalted feeling different, and even in some niche cases Solars not quite being able to get the same outcome as quickly or as easily. I'm just trying to control expectations here. Solars are not the guys who are like, really straightforward, but then you come at them from this weird angle that really trips them up and that's why Lunars are just as good as they are, only in a different way.<br /> <br /> That way lies disappointment. They're not as good, there IS a tier list, explicitly Solars are at the top. Even that obsession charm you mentioned is Essence 4, so that's a pretty long ways away at the start of a typical campaign, whereas a Solar with a supernal ability can grab all the best stuff from their area of expertise right away. There is no parity here.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Solars do not have a monopoly on cool stuff. It's <i>cool </i>to be able to shed sparks off your weapon to blind your enemies, and it's <i>fun </i>to reflexively use a Feat of Demolition as you power through an obstacle. If anyone thinks that doesn't sound nearly as fun as just being more powerful, then really given the choice they shouldn't play things that aren't Solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345926#post1345926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find objectionable and concerning is when people describe the notion of two Exalted fighting as though it's like those martial arts movies where the combatants face across one another and play out the entire battle in their minds, perfectly and equally predicting all of the moves and countermoves ahead of time, and reaching an indelible conclusion that means that they don't even bother with the fight.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they do, and it just plays out exactly as they both predicted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope I don't give that impression. I've tried to be careful to mention at the end of all of my posts that luck is a factor and nothing is 100% certain. I've seen a DB princess perfect a Dawn in 3-4 rounds. He never hit her, not even once, she never missed an attack, not even once.<br /> <br /> Just don't hear that story and think &quot;Awesome! Next session when we find that Dawn caste that we've been hunting down, I'm going to tell the rest of my group to hang back, because this is personal, and I'm going to go and handle this....personally.&quot; YOU MIGHT WIN, but I wouldn't bet the life of your character on it. Even if you set things up to take advantage of your special niche abilities, Solars often have very cheap, low essence, low requirements charms that make them just as good as you there.<br /> <br /> You almost certainly don't have the advantage in that case, you're going to have to work to overcome your disadvantage in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:03:34-08:00","id":1345996,"title":"","content":"Okay, when we get to the next page in another four posts or so, I'll respond to you in detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:56:30-08:00","id":1346013,"title":"","content":"Random bit to think on with the &quot;ease&quot; by which a nation in the Octet can make Alchemicals arises when you think on the whole general longegivity thing.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals, in general, last a while. There is still what appears to be some attrtiion. Note that only a handful of full on cities exist in each Nation. There have been Alchemical Exalted for over four millennia. Yet each Naiton, including cities, probably only has about a hundred, give or take given size. In the scheme of Autochthonia, wtih millions of people living there today, with billions of lives lived throughout the centuries, each Nation in general only has right now around over 100, again, give or take. And that many of those that are current around are often not hte only life that soul's had in the Exaltation, with many having one or two predecessors before that.<br /> <br /> This means that in thousands of years and hundres of millions of lives, we only have one thousand or so current indivduals in the whole world who have Exalted, and apparently there's still enough an incentive to look for them and enough of a worry that if one is lost something super valuable gets lost. This kind of adds up to me that additonal qualifying Exalted aren't especially common there. Kind of my take, but take Yugash, whcih probalby has like, 120 Alchemicals. My bet is that assuming a healthy range of ages, your PC Circle of them in a given game might be the first mad ein a decade or two, of other batches made every decade or two. A Nation with millions of residents, and you're one of four or five people's souls who even qualified to be used <i>this</i> decade, and that soul might ahve been put in storage or on watch centuries ago.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is that in the grand scheme of things, while Alchemical Exaltations are populous, they're probably still rare, all be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T01:08:51-08:00","id":1346098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345987#post1345987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...kind of. You're certainly more likely to find enemies who are taking advantage of their own powers, that's for sure. The thing is, if you're playing a Solar, you don't really need to do that. You don't need to set up a situation where your powers work best, because they always work best. Lunars have a neat charm for when they violate a custom of a culture to reflexively roll to try and convince everyone to overlook the slight. Solars have a charm that just makes them never commit a faux pas in the first place, no roll needed.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a 2m charm to half defense penalties against an enemy, or completely ignore them from enemies with lower initiative. Solars have a charm for the same cost that ignores all penalties regardless of initiative, and rewards 1i for successfully blocking. Also it costs only 1m if Fivefold Bulwark Stance is active. Solar doesn't worry about what initiative she's at, she just puts up the barrier and it always works.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this isn't Schrodinger's Solar. If you're a Solar swordsman, you have Dipping Swallow Defense is a Melee 1, Essence 1, Zero prerequisite charm. It's just better to be a Solar, at least in terms of achieving victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds a bit like you're suggesting that, even if in practice Lunars are a bit more &quot;set up&quot; for wild environments for Solars because of themes and caste incentives, then this doesn't really matter because any advantage from being suited to an environment is quite small compared to the cumulative gap from Solar Charms coming together vs Lunar Charms coming together. (May not be what you intended, but that's seems to be the only read of your response that can make sense as seeming to follow on from my comment? Otherwise it would be kind of a non-sequitur response?).<br /> <br /> That seems less than ideal, as would hope there was a serious &quot;off terrain&quot; / environment penalty rather than stuff which generally is just better or worse without caring about context, but getting this right is a hard problem, and I don't really want to get too into the detail of how strong a vast array of possible multiple interacting Solar Charms that can occur in a huge variety of combinations are vs their Lunar equivalents (if that is even a solvable question at all!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:52:43-08:00","id":1346139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345890#post1345890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a tangent to that, my impression would be that (if 3e Lunars balance has gone as it should!) this is true... but that the Solar player has had to build for that quite strongly, and the incentives of Solar Caste and archetypes probably don't generally push for that</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no.<br /> <br /> A Solar swordfighter is buying Dipping Swallow Defence because it's an Essence 1, Melee 1 Charm with no prereqs. They're buying that Charm to be a better swordfighter. The fact that it eliminates all environmental penalties and lets them play Lunars at their own game is just gravy.<br /> <br /> Now where Lunars have a &quot;genuine&quot; advantage is in being a Jack-Of-All-Trades. A Solar can build to be a Jack-Of-All-Trades, but you have &quot;to build for that quite strongly&quot; and &quot;the incentives of Solar Caste and archetypes don't push for that&quot;. Lunars are good with a bow, and good with their fists, and good with their horns, and good with a sword. Solars have to work to cover all those bases. But you can't use a sword and a bow at the same time, and the Solar swordsman is going to be better <i>at combat</i> than the Lunar generalist. Look at the reason why you're using a sword or a bow (to kill your enemies, to protect your friends, to provide food for your family, to overthrow tyranny), and the Solar is going to be better at achieving that goal. Always.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346098#post1346098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds a bit like you're suggesting that, even if in practice Lunars are a bit more &quot;set up&quot; for wild environments for Solars because of themes and caste incentives, then this doesn't really matter because any advantage from being suited to an environment is quite small compared to the cumulative gap from Solar Charms coming together vs Lunar Charms coming together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346098#post1346098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems less than ideal, as would hope there was a serious &quot;off terrain&quot; / environment penalty</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, Solar Charms are so much better than Lunar Charms, that increasing the environmental penalties actually makes Solars acting &quot;off terrain&quot; <i>even better</i>.<br /> <br /> Solar Charms (like Hardship Surviving Medicant Spirit, Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise, Dipping Swallow Defence) typically let you ignore <i>all penalties</i> no matter what the source is.<br /> <br /> Lunar Charms (and Dragon-Blooded Charms) let you reduce some of the penality from a limited number of &quot;in theme&quot; sources. At best this lets them break even with Solars if they are in their area of expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T06:24:15-08:00","id":1346143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346098#post1346098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if in practice Lunars are a bit more &quot;set up&quot; for wild environments for Solars because of themes and caste incentives, then this doesn't really matter because any advantage from being suited to an environment is quite small compared to the cumulative gap from Solar Charms coming together vs Lunar Charms coming together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essentially correct. Solars have a bit of a running theme in their charmset that might be cheekily described as \u201cOkay but I don\u2019t care tho.\u201d<br /> <br /> Solars can\u2019t fly, for example. They can\u2019t just leap off the ground like Superman and hover around at their heart\u2019s content like an athletic focused DB, or a Lunar with a hummingbird form can do. So you might think that against other flying enemies you\u2019d rather be a DB or a Lunar. Except Solar charms like Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Eagle Wing Style and several others just let a Solar fight flying enemies anyway. They can\u2019t fly...but they don\u2019t need to in most cases. A Solar can\u2019t submerge herself in water and transmit her senses to any other point in that body of water, hearing things from beside a bandit camp as though she were sat right at that lakeshore like an awareness focused DB can...but instead she has charms that just let her hear a conversation from miles away regardless of terrain.<br /> <br /> Now, awareness focused DB vs a Solar who barely even has any dots in it? No contest the DB wins. It\u2019s just if you want to be the best at perceiving things it\u2019s Solar all the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346139#post1346139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can't use a sword and a bow at the same time, and the Solar swordsman is going to be better <i>at combat</i> than the Lunar generalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much like this. The thing is, it can be really fun to be a Lunar generalist with access to every kind of fighting style. It\u2019s not something a Solar will ever match you in. There might even be some cases where the situation really demands for archery when you\u2019d considered yourself more of a swordsman, and in that case the Lunar may have an advantage, all Solar fighters have Eagle Wing Style, but it will be the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:25:35-08:00","id":1346151,"title":"","content":"Also this is just charm stuff I\u2019m talking about. Solars are, I think by far, the most disadvantaged setting wise. The Lunars have their schools, elders to mentor them and help them find eachother, Sidereals have Heaven and the Bureay of Destiny like dovine FBI agents with Mulder and Scully levels of freedom, and DBs rule the world, all while Solars are scattered, young and hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:46:08-08:00","id":1346169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346143#post1346143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, awareness focused DB vs a Solar who barely even has any dots in it? No contest the DB wins. It\u2019s just if you want to be the best at perceiving things it\u2019s Solar all the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> A Deeb with 5 dots and a Specialty, with one Charm is throwing 17 dice when acting in their area of expertise, and 15 dice on everything else.<br /> <br /> A Solar with just three dots in Awareness and a single Charm is throwing 16 dice with double 9s.<br /> <br /> In the Deebs area of expertise they're almost, not quite on par with a Solar. Otherwise they're blown away.<br /> <br /> This is much worse for abilities like Craft. Craft sits with Earth Aspect Dragon-Blooded who can, with a Charm, work stone without tools, or speed up their work on stone when using tools. A Solar throws more dice than the Deeb, can work without tools, ALSO speeds up the time, AND speeds up their work faster than the Deeb <b><u>AND</u></b> can not only do this with stone, but with any material. At the &quot;single Charm&quot; level, the specailist Deeb is throwing 11 dice when working within a niche of stone working (for example, working marble), and 10 dice for other stone work, and 5 dice with no magical bonuses on other Crafts. A Solar swordsmith, <b>with no dots</b> in stone working, is throwing 10 dice, doesn't need tools and is working faster than the Deeb. That Solar Swordsmith is throwing 21 dice (maintaining all the aforementioned magical benefits) when doing the thing she is good at.<br /> <br /> Solars outside of their niche are better than other specailists in their niche.<br /> <br /> If you want to carve the finest marble figures in Creation, you could be an Earth Aspected DB who specailises in marble and has maxed out their Craft skill... and still be outclassed by a Solar baker who doesn't know the sharp end of a chisel (and only has three dots in Craft: Tiger Bread and a single Charm).<br /> <br /> That gap isn't insurmountable. Give the Deeb two or three extra Charms, maybe throw in some Essence 2 Charms, and your Deeb can <i>now</i> outclass a minimally invested Solar (so long as your sticking to a very tight, in theme niche). <br /> <br /> An Elder Dragon-Blooded with literally every Awareness Charm can, indeed, outperform a Solar with zero dots of Awareness. I don't contest that. But a Solar with a <i>minimal</i> investment is going to provide stiff opposition.<br /> <br /> Sticking with your example of Awareness, the Essence 3 Experienced Dragon-Blooded in the Corebook is throwing a mighty 11 dice on &quot;senses&quot; rolls (when they max their Excellency). An Essence 1 starting Solar can match that with ease. In fact every single Essence 1 Solar in Tomb of Dreams beats that. Even Volfer (who rolls a rather pathetic 12 dice). A mental tertiary Solar who doesn't favor Awareness could trivially match 11 dice. And 11 dice is really good for a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Berit and Mnemon, Essence 5 daughters of the Scarlet Empress, roll 14 dice -- the highest of any published Dragon-Blooded (Awareness is an Aspect ability for Mnemon -- she's got 5 dots in it). The same as Faka Kun, Essence 1 acrobat, starting level Solar. Oops, sorry, Faka Kun rolls <i>19 dice</i> (is built <i>below</i> the level of a starting Solar and has <i>no</i> Awareness Charms except the Excellency). Iay Selak Amu and Karal Fire Orchid (also Essence 1 Solars built below the level of starting characters) roll 14 dice. And none of these Solars have Awareness Charms beyond the Excellency.<br /> <br /> And, again, let me be clear that I'm pitting Elder, Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded <i>in fields they are good at</i> against <i>below starting level</i> Solars who don't have any relevant Charms apart from the Excellency. And the Solars are still as good, if not better. (Except Volfer. Because Volfer sucks.)<br /> <br /> (Mnemon can, at least, ride the senses of others and detect hidden threats with double 9s if they're at short range and standing on a stone floor. Which, you know, is something. Even if a Solar can get double 9s on all Awareness rolls peroid with an Essence 1 Charm with no prereqs. The three Solars who match her are missing 5 Charms. Give Faka Kun Sensory Acuity Prana and she's straight-up better at Awareness than the strongest Deeb in the game. Enjoy that. Then spend your other 4 Charms.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-05-2019, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:15:58-08:00","id":1346178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346169#post1346169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh.<br /> <br /> A Deeb with 5 dots and a Specialty, with one Charm is throwing 17 dice when acting in their area of expertise, and 15 dice on everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t exactly just thinking about dice. DBs especially don\u2019t really do the insane amounts of dice thing anyway. I was thinking more like comparing a Solar with 14 dice to a DB with Horizon Spanning Echos. Where one can say \u201clisten for the voice of my adversary, the anathema known as Final Ray.\u201d And then when he enters the city incognito and gets asked his business by the gate guard, the Air Aspect suddenly snaps to the rest of the Hearth in the palace and says \u201cFinal Ray is here, at the South Gate.\u201d It\u2019s not really comparable to having 14 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:44:52-08:00","id":1346188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346178#post1346178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn\u2019t exactly just thinking about dice. DBs especially don\u2019t really do the insane amounts of dice thing anyway. I was thinking more like comparing a Solar with 14 dice to a DB with Horizon Spanning Echos. Where one can say \u201clisten for the voice of my adversary, the anathema known as Final Ray.\u201d And then when he enters the city incognito and gets asked his business by the gate guard, the Air Aspect suddenly snaps to the rest of the Hearth in the palace and says \u201cFinal Ray is here, at the South Gate.\u201d It\u2019s not really comparable to having 14 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>How big is this city?<br /> <br /> Because if the South Gate is a mile away then the Solar can totally do that with Unsurpassed Hearing and Touch Technique. <br /> <br /> If it's three miles away, they'll have to use Unsurpassed Taste and Smell to track their quarry by scent instead.<br /> <br /> Granted Horizon Spanning Echos works to (Essence) miles. So an Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded can listen in further than a Solar can scent. But again, what's the goal? If you want to find Final Ray, a Solar is going to find them first, simply by throwing buckets of dice at the problem.<br /> <br /> But to address your point, it's not about dice. It's about what you can do with your Charms. Instead of throwing 17 dice, that Deeb could hear through walls or ignore certain environmental penalties. The Solar with 16 dice and double 9s is probably still better at hearing things on the other side of a stone wall and is definitely better at seeing through a sandstorm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-05-2019, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:46:44-08:00","id":1346189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346188#post1346188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How big is this city?<br /> <br /> Because if the South Gate is a mile away then the Solar can totally do that with Unsurpassed Hearing and Touch Technique. <br /> <br /> If it's three miles away, they'll have to use Unsurpassed Taste and Smell to track their quarry by scent instead.<br /> <br /> Granted Horizon Spanning Echos works to (Essence) miles. So an Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded can listen in further than a Solar can scent. But again, what's the goal? If you want to find Final Ray, a Solar is going to find them first, simply by throwing buckets of dice at the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>A solar with Awareness 3 doesn\u2019t have Unsurpassed anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:57:51-08:00","id":1346192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346143#post1346143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is essentially correct. Solars have a bit of a running theme in their charmset that might be cheekily described as \u201cOkay but I don\u2019t care tho.\u201d<br /> <br /> Solars can\u2019t fly, for example. They can\u2019t just leap off the ground like Superman and hover around at their heart\u2019s content like an athletic focused DB, or a Lunar with a hummingbird form can do. So you might think that against other flying enemies you\u2019d rather be a DB or a Lunar. Except Solar charms like Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Eagle Wing Style and several others just let a Solar fight flying enemies anyway. They can\u2019t fly...but they don\u2019t need to in most cases. A Solar can\u2019t submerge herself in water and transmit her senses to any other point in that body of water, hearing things from beside a bandit camp as though she were sat right at that lakeshore like an awareness focused DB can...but instead she has charms that just let her hear a conversation from miles away regardless of terrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit unusual compared to my expectation. Solars being culture heroes who are from particular environments and cultures in fairly signature ways, it's seem unusual that their powers are sort of... indifferent to their environment, such that a Solar master of the deep forest's powers don't really care about where he is, rather than interacting in specific ways that are step up for him (and a step down when he doesn't have that environment), and that a player whose image of a Solar is the master of the deep desert or an urbane creature of the city finds they aren't really better in any of those locales than players who don't build that way.<br /> <br /> I suppose that is perhaps to avoid issues of being locale locked though, as that complaint is bad enough with Sail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:10:21-08:00","id":1346196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346189#post1346189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A solar with Awareness 3 doesn\u2019t have Unsurpassed anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I freely concede that an invested Exalt will have powers an uninvested Exalt doesn't have.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't really say anything about the dynamics between the Exalted. <br /> <br /> A Deeb who has invested in Awareness will have neat tricks that a Solar who hasn't invested will lack. But that's equally true vice versa.<br /> <br /> The issue for me is that the uninvested Solar is still absolutely amazing at Awareness, beyond all mortal skill and is probably better than an invested Deeb at straightforward applications of skill. Whilst the uninvested Deeb is no better than Joe Average Mortal.<br /> <br /> (That an invested Solar be better than an invested Deeb is a feature, not a bug. An invested Solar should be better than an invested Deeb. But an invested Deeb shouldn't have to be looking for Essence 3 niches to outshine an uninvested Solar. Thems the breaks, I guess. That Awareness 3 Solar is still finding Final Ray before you, even if they can't copy your trick.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-05-2019, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:11:07-08:00","id":1346197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346192#post1346192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that is perhaps to avoid issues of being locale locked though, as that complaint is bad enough with Sail.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not just environment stuff, that\u2019s just an easy one to point to. There\u2019s also styles and themes and stuff. Like the Lunar charms that trigger off your opponent being lower initiative where the Solar ones always work at their best, or charms where other exalted have to make a roll but Solars just automatically succeed with theirs. Like the charm Perfect Mirror, which allows a Solar to make a disguise in a single action which is utterly impenetrable to even magical senses, and even copies the animal of different types of exalt. The only way to pierce it is by the Solar behaving in a grossly out of character way, in which case supernatural viewers have to make the roll at -4 or -5 dice, when the solar made hers with (Essence) Non-charm automatic successes, and double 9s at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:15:13-08:00","id":1346199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346196#post1346196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue for me is that the uninvested Solar is still absolutely amazing at Awareness, beyond all mortal skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;uninvested,&quot; you mean &quot;has Charms in, or has Favored the Ability representing an affinity for the skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bKind of an odd definition of &quot;uninvested.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:18:04-08:00","id":1346200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346196#post1346196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I freely concede that an invested Exalt will have powers an uninvested Exalt doesn't have.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't really say anything about the dynamics between the Exalted. <br /> <br /> A Deeb who has invested in Awareness will have neat tricks that a Solar who hasn't invested will lack. But that's equally true vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>The quote you were responding to was me saying that a dedicated DB will outclass a Solar who barely has any dots in the ability. Solars are awesome, they\u2019re not so awesome that they can totally overrun a DB by taking a random Ability 2 charm with no pre-reqs. Your Twilight with Dipping Swallow and Fire and Stones Strike is going to get rolled by Cathak Cainen.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, the twilight has a legion of clockwork soldiers or whatever whatever, the point is you don\u2019t just get to automatically beat anyone with a barest thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:31:47-08:00","id":1346202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346197#post1346197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not just environment stuff, that\u2019s just an easy one to point to. There\u2019s also styles and themes and stuff. Like the Lunar charms that trigger off your opponent being lower initiative where the Solar ones always work at their best, or charms where other exalted have to make a roll but Solars just automatically succeed with theirs. Like the charm Perfect Mirror, which allows a Solar to make a disguise in a single action which is utterly impenetrable to even magical senses, and even copies the animal of different types of exalt. The only way to pierce it is by the Solar behaving in a grossly out of character way, in which case supernatural viewers have to make the roll at -4 or -5 dice, when the solar made hers with (Essence) Non-charm automatic successes, and double 9s at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those kind of feel like a different kettle of fish because those relate to intricacies of an abstract resource in the combat system or abstracted dice rolls, and don't tell you anything inherently. (There isn't really anything to &quot;map&quot; them to, exactly, and may be better or worse depending wholly on the integer values involved! Numbers move slightly differently in an abstracted minigame.). While powers that present limited interactions with and dependencies on environment, or which don't, does quite differently set up a character who feel like they can or can't meaningfully play as if they are an archetype that is linked to thriving in a particular environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:47:01-08:00","id":1346206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346199#post1346199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;uninvested,&quot; you mean &quot;has Charms in, or has Favored the Ability representing an affinity for the skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bKind of an odd definition of &quot;uninvested.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One Charm is invested to you?<br /> <br /> A character who takes one Ox-body Technique is invested in Resistance?<br /> <br /> I like to play devil's advocate, so I don't fault you for trying, but I'm <i>super</i>-comfortable calling one Charm &quot;uninvested&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346200#post1346200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Twilight with Dipping Swallow and Fire and Stones Strike is going to get rolled by Cathak Cainen.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, the twilight has a legion of clockwork soldiers or whatever whatever</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge accepted.<br /> <br /> I'm going to make a Twilight who only knows those three Charms from combat abilities and play that out against Cainan (sans battlegroup and bodyguard -- Solar's aren't that tough.) Heck, let's keep it <i>vaguely</i> interesting -- I won't use the Belt of Shadow Walking, and I'll make her Mental Primary.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Ok, overwhelming Fire Majesty Stance is brutal. Point taken. Could still nail him with the Belt though. Or TAP -- Scrappy The Three Charm Twilight opened with an 8 Lethal alpha strike that totally would have aced Cainan if I'd cheesed TAP into the build, but it seemed against the spirit of the challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-05-2019, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:50:34-08:00","id":1346208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346206#post1346206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm is invested to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it's one-fifteenth of your starting Charms? I'm just saying I wouldn't call it <i>un</i>invested.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:52:21-08:00","id":1346209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346206#post1346206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Challenge accepted.<br /> <br /> I'm going to make a Twilight who only knows those two Charms from combat abilities and play that out against Cainan (sans battlegroup and bodyguard -- Solar's aren't that tough.) Heck, let's keep it <i>vaguely</i> interesting -- I won't use the Belt of Shadow Walking, and I'll make her Mental Primary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don\u2019t forget that as a QC Cainen doesn\u2019t have a lower dice pool for his decisive attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:12:45-08:00","id":1346221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1345982#post1345982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're shifting the goalposts away from &quot;read what's in the book&quot; to &quot;I don't actually buy into what the book depicts&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, on top of Lux consistently being portrayed as quite the little giant city diva, and the idea of a grandiose hero opting for a dramatic and showy method over the practical one (see <b>the very fact that Lux has paramagnetic catapults in the first place </b> as opposed to... bridges), you're just kind of overlooking details such as it being a described as a last resort tactic at a time when the city's usual defences had been shut down (a good faith reading of that might conclude that flinging regular projectiles was off the table) and, again, Estasia was facing a war that was unlike the norm for conflict within the limiting confines of the Realm of Brass and Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds a lot like &quot;I don't agree with you, but I do agree with you&quot;. Which is it? Was Lux flattening a raiding party or was he flattening an invading force that could threaten his security and his people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hard is good enough to make something uncommon. </div> </div> </div>Uncommon multiplied by thousands of years equals plenty of examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And always failed. </div> </div> </div>You are missing the point that the Octet has had many reasons and plenty of time to develop the same sorts of logistical practices we've seen developed in the real world. The German military in World War 2 went from centralized tank repair at German factories to a developed and decentralized doctrine of forward operating depots by the end of the war, largely due to circumstances analogous to what the Octet would have to deal with, such as round-trip travel times and logistical problems like disconnected rail lines.<br /> <br /> Whether the wars were successful or not means little to the incentive structure to find ways to ameliorate the challenges a people are facing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't come out of every wall, and even if it did, that wouldn't mean there is no value in possessing a surplus while also denying rivals the same. </div> </div> </div>You are thinking of nutrient slurry like a farm. It isn't. It's like a river. The only way to deny it to your rivals is to divert it entirely. Such things are easier said than done, especially if you want to divert it to your own territory. That's a major infrastructure project in hostile territory, justifying the need for extended logistics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, of barrels of slurry are easier to carry then pallets of steel, and you steal them from people that will pay you steel to get back the slurry (because people need to eat every day and time spent increasing production of slurry is time taken away from some other industry), which might the raiders go for? </div> </div> </div>I don't think you've thought this through. If there's barrels sitting around somewhere, you are either dealing with some outpost community that exists for a specific purpose and is being supplied by delivery due to distance from the most convenient nutrient slurry tap or you are dealing with surplus stored against disruptions of normal supply - a surplus that exists because the community produces enough to eat and then some. Only the first group is likely to negotiate and only if they do not have enough remaining to tide them over until the next supply delivery through some measure of rationing. Also, what's to stop them from shooting you when you come to make the exchange? After all, they'll know where you'll be, they'll have time to bring in reinforcements, and a raid often relies upon the element of surprise to be successful.<br /> <br /> Besides which, barrels of nutrient slurry are probably one of the lightest things you are likely to get through raiding and they are still going to be hefty. Liquids like water are a kilogram a liter or over 8 lbs a gallon, making a twenty gallon drum of slurry somewhere in the range of 150 lbs. If you get lucky it might be bales of cloth that you seize - the Octet do have ways of producing that - but a lack of new clothes is less compelling than a lack of food, so that's going to be lower priority on your &quot;take stuff and then sell it back to them&quot; plan.<br /> <br /> Any which way you slice it, you'll need to move a large volume of goods from where you can get them and off to where you can use them, so you are looking at wagons, carts, trains, trams, etc. that need guarded until the plunder is shipped home. While that happens, you'll have an army in the field in hostile territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Excavated? Why are they attacking mines instead of warehouses? </div> </div> </div>Because mines aren't located inside sentient cities that can have automated defense grids. Outlying warehouses will be near the mines and only have enough space to store what's going to be shipped to the factories on the next tram if the system is in any way optimized, maybe a little more if they have surplus production that will be eventually result in a double shipment. If you want more than a few days worth of stuff, you'll have to hold on to it and work it yourself, just like has happened in every modern real-world war. Want oil? Well, the enemy isn't going to work the derricks for you once they are dead or run off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shorter supply lines are generally why you don't want to be locked down in one place. If you're going after something that will take long enough to load up that enemies will surround you, you're doing residing incorrectly. </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean &quot;raiding&quot; not &quot;residing&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's why real-world raids are over things that were mobile in some way. You seized wagons of goods, livestock, slaves, or small high-value items like gold coins or silver plates. However, Autochthonia largely doesn't have livestock, slavery doesn't get any mention that I can recall, they don't really buy into the idea of value beyond utility, and internal transit systems are more akin to trains than wagons and so not easily diverted. Smash-and-grab raiding isn't a thing that functions well in Autochthonia on the scale of the Eight Nations and the conflicts between them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, it's not as if we lack historical example of this. Vikings, Saracens, the Anglo-Scottish border, pastoral nomads out of China's northern frontier, all examples of societies that enriched themselves on a sustained process of using high mobility and good planning to get in, grab lots of valuable materials and people, then get out before an enemy force could be mobilised against them and cut off their line of retreat. </div> </div> </div>Note the small size of the groups doing the raiding for small volumes of stuff. One man can carry away enough to feed himself for weeks or a tribe for days, but not a nation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, in many of these cases, sustained campaigns of raising gradually evolved into straight up colonisation, but the Scandinavians were a bit dependent on things like Britain not eventually being completely inaccessible from Scandinavia. It also being a lot more accessible owing to the fact that there is a while sea to sail across, rather than being to approach via tunnels. </div> </div> </div>So in other words, raiding for small volumes of goods only works if you can hit whenever you want, easily move what you take, and can be relatively immune to reprisal. Not things that apply to city-dwelling nations, nor the kinds of resources that said nations want, nor to the terrain that the Octet live in. Instead, their warfare over resources is going to require that they get substantial amounts of resources out of the venture, require significant manpower to mount the expedition, and require a period of time spent fending off reprisals (because as long as you can reach them, they can reach you). In short, it's going to be a war and require logistical planning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, some kinds of operations. Lightning raids still function today, facilitated by things like planes. They're not concerned with the acquisition of commodities, but their opposition have advantages that Autochthonians will generally lack, such as wider implementation of more accurate and destructive ranged weaponry. </div> </div> </div>The fact that modern raids aren't about resources means that they aren't comparable except in duration of initial combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alchemicals can be the military equivalent of a lot of things. Sometimes they're commandos, where you outfit them for stealth, speed and precision that increases the time they can stay ahead of and harass enemies before they need to go back to the vats. Maybe they sometimes go outfitted for maximum destruction because the person planning the raid decided to go for a blitzkrieg approach, all &quot;go in and obliterate everything, sustain fire while the troops pick up the goods and then fall back&quot;. Maybe there's an Alchemical build that is the equivalent of anti-armour rockets, but if it takes three days for them to get there then a viable tactic is to not be there anymore. Retreat into those tunnels that are hard to be followed into and easier to set traps in. Perhaps use your blasty powers to cave in the entrance. </div> </div> </div>You missed the equivalency. They are the equivalent of tanks because they are high-power assets that require regular maintenance and upkeep if you expect them to function at optimal capacity for extended lengths of time. Your commando eventually needs to come back because the mission is accomplished or irrelevant and once he does you need to refit him if you don't immediately have another commando thing to do. You can try to do a blitzkrieg thing with a commando, but it won't work as well, much like a tank that's got some holes in the armor or a gun that's jamming. If you have to send your Alchemical all the way back to the factory for refit, you incur tons of logistical overhead in the field use of Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compass: Autochthonian depicts a world where a fairly uniform resource constraint is the inability to mobilise the vats needed for Exalted to respec, so they need to plan around that. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it does a poor job of depicting warfare between the Eight Nations with any level of substantial detail beyond &quot;they use crossbows as primary weapons&quot; and &quot;they use magitech stuff and Alchemicals&quot;. About the only place that it is actually addresses the question of building vats complexes outside cities is the sidebar about building them in Creation, where the stuff mentioned is for a full sized complex capable of servicing arbitrary numbers of Champions and Collosi. Something in the field, able to service one Alchemical at a time, has significantly smaller power and resource needs.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the entry for blightborn, IIRC, mentions that they often find ways to build vats complexes in blight zones, guided to service Apostate Alchemicals, establishing that vats can be created in Autochthonia outside of Alchemical cities (a thing we also know because the first Alchemicals were built before there were Alchemical cities). A mobile vat option, either a standalone set of artifact gear or a Collossus Charm usable only by Champions, would fit fairly seamlessly into the setting without disrupting the existing depictions of Autochthonian warfare, provided there was some level of time constraint on setup and redeployment of such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's going to be hard in any event to have pitched battles in this world, there is often not the room. </div> </div> </div>I don't expect pitched battles, although there is apparently often room. Various nations inhabit cavities measured in the miles, especially Claslat, Nurad, and Jarish, and those aren't depicted as bizarre oddities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:38:01-08:00","id":1346231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346208#post1346208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it's one-fifteenth of your starting Charms? I'm just saying I wouldn't call it <i>un</i>invested.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Insert meme about Shaggy using nearly 7% of his power*<br /> <br /> Damn, now I've foiled my own argument. You win this round Count!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:25:43-08:00","id":1346239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346206#post1346206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, overwhelming Fire Majesty Stance is brutal. Point taken. Could still nail him with the Belt though. Or TAP -- Scrappy The Three Charm Twilight opened with an 8 Lethal alpha strike that totally would have aced Cainan if I'd cheesed TAP into the build, but it seemed against the spirit of the challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there was a challenge issued TAP and Belt of Shadow Walking would both definitely be off limits. So would combat evocations, and arguably artifact weapons and armor.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m talking about a character that went super hard into medicine to become the greatest physician in the world, and picked up a charm or two in melee so they could contribute a little there. Not one who has 5 melee, combat specialties, a bunch of combat charms from non-combat abilities, or abuses dematerialization mechanics in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:32:49-08:00","id":1346243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346202#post1346202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those kind of feel like a different kettle of fish because those relate to intricacies of an abstract resource in the combat system or abstracted dice rolls, and don't tell you anything inherently. (There isn't really anything to &amp;quot;map&amp;quot; them to, exactly, and may be better or worse depending wholly on the integer values involved! Numbers move slightly differently in an abstracted minigame.). While powers that present limited interactions with and dependencies on environment, or which don't, does quite differently set up a character who feel like they can or can't meaningfully play as if they are an archetype that is linked to thriving in a particular environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The combat abilities that map to initiative aren\u2019t just things out of nowhere that are fun game mechanics, necessarily. Lunars are rewarded for being the predator, not the prey. When they\u2019re winning, have their enemy on the back step, cornering their dinner, then their charms work better. The Solar disguise is just impenetrable perfection. Almost to the point of being completely useless to try and see past it, that\u2019s not how you\u2019ll catch them, if you do at all. Instead look at actions, motives, and the few things that their disguise can\u2019t replicate. Even a Solar disguised as a Lunar can\u2019t shapeshift, for example. That\u2019s what I think the numbers are implying there.<br /> <br /> Although if you\u2019re looking to play an experience as a culture hero with a home turf that makes them better, stronger, and seems to empower them with the people and the land, go Lunar. They\u2019re SO about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:31:02-08:00","id":1346258,"title":"","content":"Couple comments (mainly just because I feel like I want to respond to your post more than I guess I'm contributing to the thread at this point):<br /> <br /> To flesh out a bit about what I mean by the other examples being more abstracted and that feeling different, is that there is so much more latitude to interpretation. You could certainly interpret that mechanic as having a predatory vibe and being useful to portray a hero with a heroic yet slightly perhaps sinister and predatory feel (that's an interesting connection), but you could also use it to portray a hero who is simply strong and brave and thrives on having the advantage. There's nothing necessary about that connection, or literal about that mechanic. This is pretty much a tangent though, and may be more of a difference of degree than kind!<br /> <br /> Separately, on playing a Lunar to play a &quot;<i>hero with a home turf that makes them better, stronger, and seems to empower them with the people and the land</i>&quot;, this is where it kind of feels to me like I want to protest that this should be possible within a Solar's aesthetic and story. But! This is probably where even *very* flexible character types as in Exalted run up against limits, and that's just kind of the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:56:34-08:00","id":1346295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345693-alchemicals-vs-solars-and-other-creation-exalts?p=1346258#post1346258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separately, on playing a Lunar to play a &quot;<i>hero with a home turf that makes them better, stronger, and seems to empower them with the people and the land</i>&quot;, this is where it kind of feels to me like I want to protest that this should be possible within a Solar's aesthetic and story. But! This is probably where even *very* flexible character types as in Exalted run up against limits, and that's just kind of the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it totally is possible as a Solar. If you've got a concept for a character, 99% of the time a Solar can do it. That's one of the reasons they're the corebook splat. A decent amount of Solar charms involve intimacies, like Fists of Iron Technique, that gets bonus damage if you're striking a hated foe, defending a beloved friend, or simply enjoy the thrill of punching. You could easily use your intimacy to defend your home or your people in that and it would make you stronger by virtue of defending your home.<br /> <br /> It's not really the same though, because you could be using any intimacy for that, and there's ones that are probably a lot easier to apply more of the time, depending on where you are.<br /> <br /> You could always write your own charms that do, of course. Especially especially if you end up getting to Essence 6+, those can start to break out of the mold of &quot;Solar charms&quot; and much more into &quot;Charms for just my character.&quot; The only thing really holding you back is balance. Solar charms are already the absolute limit of Exalted power, so any you make shouldn't really be any stronger than the ones printed, but you also probably want to make them competitive with the printed ones too. Nobody wants to buy a charm that just performs worse in some situations for no benefit.<br /> <br /> It's a fine line to walk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}